Hallo Alex,

I am forwarding an email from Northgate Logistics about their invoice 4471 =
(attached). We paid it short in September because two pallets of impellers =
arrived damaged in the August shipment to Dortmund, and we deducted the val=
ue of the damaged parts, EUR 2,800.00. Northgate now say the deduction was =
never agreed, and they will put our account on stop if we do not pay the ba=
lance within 7 days.

Can you tell me how to answer them? I am not sure whether this is a legal q=
uestion or one for procurement, but I did not want to ignore it.

Viele Gr=C3=BC=C3=9Fe / Kind regards
Lena

Lena Vogt
Finance Manager
Kestrel Pumpen GmbH
Dortmund, Germany
lena.vogt@kestrel-eng.de

-----Urspr=C3=BCngliche Nachricht-----
Von: Northgate Logistics Accounts <accounts@northgate-logistics.com>
Gesendet: Donnerstag, 15. Oktober 2026 17:42
An: Lena Vogt <lena.vogt@kestrel-eng.de>
Betreff: Northgate Logistics - invoice 4471 short payment

Dear Ms Vogt,

Our records show a payment of EUR 15,840.00 received on 25 September 2026 a=
gainst invoice 4471 dated 31 August 2026 for EUR 18,640.00. A balance of EU=
R 2,800.00 remains outstanding.

We have no record of agreeing a deduction for damaged goods. Under clause 1=
4 of our standard trading conditions, any claim for loss of or damage to go=
ods in transit must be notified in writing within 7 days of delivery, and u=
nder clause 18 claims may not be set off against our charges.

Please arrange payment of the balance within 7 days of this email. If we do=
 not receive payment, we will charge interest under our terms and may place=
 your account on stop, which would affect the collections booked for Novemb=
er.

Kind regards

Accounts Receivable
Northgate Logistics Ltd
accounts@northgate-logistics.com

